[Music]  area hikers are getting ready for a big  event to help raise money for  Make-A-Wish but for one family every  step they take on the hike as a reminder  of how One Wish can be life-changing for  children who are trying to live life to  the fullest Victoria Saha has our story  [Applause]  the Jolly family loved to hike  and their 14 year old son Colin is  following in their footsteps except he's  following in an off-road wheelchair  really is inspiring watching Colin you  know with all the challenges that he  said to deal with just be so happy and  happy and positive Colin was born with a  rare disorder leaving him non-verbal  hour by hour make sure he's taken care  of and then we take care of ourselves  his parents Daniel and Carrie are doing  their best to give him a normal life by  exploring the outdoors  he loves it you just you see it in his  face he's looking around he's engaged  and it just it gets him out there with  everybody and he's just happy but  getting to hike as a family wasn't the  easiest as they would take turns caring  Colin and he was starting to get too big  to for me to carry on my shoulders but  last August one of Colin's doctors  nominated him for Make-A-Wish we were  planning on uh getting an off-road  wheelchair  um we started to do a bunch of research  a wheelchair that would have cost the  family five thousand dollars but make a  wish made the Jolly's wish come true  since then Colin gets to go on every  hike and Adventure from the trails of  Nevada all the way to the lakes of  Wisconsin now the family is giving back  by taking part in a 26.2 mile hike in  February all part of the trailblaze  challenge for Make-A-Wish raising as  much money as possible for these kids to  make as many kids life-changing wishes  come true is what it's really all about  so another family can know that being  physically limited doesn't have to stop  you from climbing your way through life  thank you good job buddy Victoria saw  him eight news now  Make-a-Wish runs on donations so if  you'd like to donate or take part in the  trailblaze hike that's coming up in  February we'll have that information on  our website 8newsnow.com

